px georgia,serif;margin:0 0 10px"><span>By Alicia P.Q. Wittmeyer</span></p>=
<p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"=
><span>The repression started long before it became a genocide.</span></p><=
p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px">=
<span>Myanmar is an ethnically diverse country, and for decades, the Rohing=
ya were just one ethnic group among many. They won parliamentary elections,=
 formed student unions and ran businesses.</span></p><p style=3D"font:norma=
l 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>But over time, =
the Rohingya, who are Muslim, began facing increasing crackdowns from Myanm=
ar=E2=80=99s Buddhist majority.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px=
 georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>In 1982, while the country=
 was under military rule, a restrictive citizenship law effectively rendere=
d most Rohingya stateless. By 2012, </span><a href=3D"https://nl.nytimes.co=
m/f/newsletter/BFEgKflN91_emqmvLxCUpA~~/AAAAARA~/QcV20OGKBrjrMTkGN-McGK8GRL=
f_9Nwju-cEmi3IYZphxFAw1DO4OHDIIVHSefbxKWDx7VlLgl8UBdeN7P1ZUnqKt9ZntoIas4Ufb=
nFrccr_mLBXFXaYMrGtzxaQuAN4ooX0qxI2w-G4Six_ZIU28WrQmJ5g7m0Fv29AYKAr2TnSyqWZ=
qiyoK_zwBSKNEhyomWHeCtLixkjD_ZMpCUZjXRAPROOgpfyrdYaprWhrH16ewChDr0O4pvssPcD=
oJiQUHx5YfYJ8Lmv_oIdq2nuJ5qE4YY-662pTrWgevxapYMDL7jpcodLqGGXk38xzdUW1mxYY-r=
Hn_5NEyUA2fpot5MziU3ssQfOqHGSA6ZErtJ1zUhSge3C3YAy1SiTxwW8BLNdeLQDyG4zhdtZeT=
ASXSw~~" class=3D"css-sdwaa1" style=3D"color:#286ed0;-webkit-text-decoratio=
n:underline;text-decoration:underline">as my colleagues write</a><span>:</s=
pan></p><p style=3D"font:17px/25px georgia,serif;margin:0 50px 15px;color:#=
666" class=3D"css-14jlz04"><span>They had lost their freedom of movement an=
d assembly. Their calls to prayer were silenced; many could not attend scho=
ol. Some were penned in internment camps. Others suffered village burnings =
and other pogroms.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,seri=
f;color:#333;margin:20px 0 15px"><span>But it was the events of 2016 and 20=
17 that were the court=E2=80=99s focus =E2=80=94 when Myanmar launched what=
 the court has now called a coordinated campaign to remove the Rohingya tha=
t involved killing, raping and razing villages. It succeeded: Eventually mo=
re than a million fled to neighboring Bangladesh, where they largely remain=
 today.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#33=
3;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The ruling marks the first time a country has been=
 held to account for violating the 1948 Genocide Convention.</span><span st=
yle=3D"font-weight:700"> </span><span>It has important implications =E2=80=
=94 for international law, and for the genocide case against Israel before =
the same court. It=E2=80=99s not clear, however, that the ruling will make =
a major difference in the lives of the people at the center of it =E2=80=94=
 the Rohingya.</span></p><table border=3D"0" cellpadding=3D"0" cellspacing=
=3D"0" style=3D"width:100%"><tbody><tr><td style=3D"text-align:center"><a h=
